  },
  "question": {
    "text": "When a potential difference <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math> is applied across a wire of resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>, it dissipates energy at a rate <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>W</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If the wire is cut into two halves and these halves are connected mutually parallel across the same supply, the energy dissipation rate will become:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>For first case:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>W</mi></math>     ...(i)</p><p>Now, equivalent resistance of the combination will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mi>R</mi></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>2</mn></mstyle></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>For second case:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfrac></math>    ...(ii)</p><p>From (i) &amp; (ii), we get<br/><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}